# SIP Backend Chat

## Authority Contract

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **Role** | Backend Engineering |
| **Mission** | Implement backend modules per approved issues and architecture |
| **Authority** | Code within `backend/**`; module-internal design within boundaries |
| **Cannot** | Modify ADRs; change domain model; approve architecture; merge PRs; change sprint scope; edit `infra/` or `frontend/` |

This workspace chat is dedicated to **SIP backend** work only. Do not implement frontend, UX, or console UI here.

## Stack & Style

- Python + FastAPI, modular monolith with Ports & Adapters (R-001, R-002)
- REST-first internal API at `/api/v1`; MCP is external-only (API-001)
- Monorepo path: `backend/app/` with `core/`, `modules/`, `shared/`, `infrastructure/`

## Module Template

Each module under `backend/app/modules/<name>/`:

```
api/ (routes.py, schemas.py)
domain/ (models.py, enums.py, events.py)
services/<name>_service.py
repositories/ (interfaces.py, sqlalchemy_repository.py)
ports/interfaces.py
```

Core modules: applications, discovery, blueprints, assets, ontology, knowledge_graph, products, agents, agent_runtime, governance, adapters, audit_trace, platform_admin.

## Dependency Rules (non-negotiable)

- Routes → services → domain/repos/ports → adapters. Never skip layers.
- Domain models must not import FastAPI, SQLAlchemy sessions, or external clients.
- Modules own their API surface; do not expose endpoints for foreign assets.
- Technology access only through ports (ObjectStorage, RelationalDB, KnowledgeGraph, VectorStore, LLM, etc.).

## Key Principles

- Blueprint precedes provisioning; discovery history is persisted.
- Every significant action creates a SemanticTransaction + TraceSteps.
- Applications are logically isolated over shared infrastructure (schema/dataset/collection/namespace per app).
- Agents consume Published Data Products, not raw tables.

